 3.9. Good.\n\nBut wait: `header: List[str] | None = None` is a *variable* annotation — also not evaluated at runtime under PEP 563? Actually PEP 563 makes all annotations strings, including local variable annotations (they're not even stored for locals). Module-level and class-level variable annotations are stored in __annotations__ as strings. So fine.\n\nHowever, `Optional[Sequence[str]]` in cli.py signature → change to `Sequence[str] | None`.\n\nLet me modernize: use `collections.abc` imports for Iterable/Sequence, and builtin generics. Also remove the unused `List` import. Also add `check=False` explicitly to subprocess.run. Also sort `__all__` (RUF022).\n\nPython version target: with builtin generics in annotations + future import, runtime works on 3.7+ (actually `list[str]` inside `typing.get_type_hints` would fail on 3.8, but we never call that). I'll declare requires-python >= 3.9 in pyproject. Let me also check `dict` usage — none.\n\nAlso note: `from __future__ import annotations` is needed for `X | None` annotations on 3.9 — present.\n\nLet me apply the edits.\n\nAlso in core.py, `from typing import Iterable, List, Sequence, Tuple` → `from collections.abc import Iterable, Sequence`.\n\nLet me rewrite the import sections and annotations.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e60bb3a3001sOgFGkWDgvj8qa","sessionID":"ses_e19f61cd3ffejcCABau2G12ZL0","messageID":"msg_1e60ba559001AzXWK11kQlZf5o"}}
